# Keep the SkyPilot workdir upload small. Both training and eval jobs ship this
# tree as their code: `workdir: .` uploads it per job, so the pod runs the exact
# snapshot that was submitted and a preemption restart re-runs the same code.
# Everything excluded here is either already on the pod or belongs on NFS/S3:
# the PyRep/RLBench forks live in the eval image (/opt/src/PyRep2,
# /opt/src/RLBench2), the venv lives on NFS, and datasets and checkpoints are
# read from NFS (training) or S3 (eval) at runtime. The result is ~2 MB.
#
# Every directory pattern is anchored with a leading slash. An unanchored `data`
# matches at any depth and silently drops `config/data/`, which Hydra needs to
# compose `data/single` — the eval then dies with MissingConfigException.
#
# Note what is NOT excluded: the root `data/` package. It is 350 KB of tracked
# Python (data.generation / data.processing, imported by the orbital eval and the
# zarr converters), not a dataset directory. The zarr datasets it produces live
# under /k8s-nfs/harsvbha/3dfa/data and were never in this tree.
/.git
/PyRep
/RLBench
/logs
/train_logs
/eval_logs
/debug_videos
/results
/paper
/plots
/docker
/.venv
/.pytest_cache
/wandb
/3dfa_data
*.rrd
*.pth
*.pt
*.zip
*.out
*.log
__pycache__
*.egg-info
